    affiliation: Monterey Bay Aquarium Research Institute (MBARI)
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TO VERIFY
  - given-names: John
    name-particle: P.
    family-names: Ryan
    affiliation: Monterey Bay Aquarium Research Institute (MBARI)
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'   # TO VERIFY
repository-code: 'https://github.com/duane-edgington/perch-hoplite-orcas-MBNMS'
abstract: >-
  Code, trained classifiers, expert-confirmed labels, and a
  reproducibility bundle for detecting Bigg's (transient) killer whale
  vocalizations in the MBARI MARS cabled hydrophone archive. The method
  applies agile modeling with a human-in-the-loop labeling loop to a
  linear probe trained on frozen Google Perch V2 audio embeddings.
  Validation uses a permanently held-out test month (May 2018).
keywords:
  - passive acoustic monitoring
  - bioacoustics
  - killer whale
  - Orcinus orca
  - Bigg's killer whale
  - Perch V2
  - agile modeling
  - foundation model
  - MBARI MARS
  - Monterey Bay National Marine Sanctuary
